          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Well groomed, appears tired and mildly tense; intermittently impatient and checking phone for work messages."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-26",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-26",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mental status examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Alert and oriented to person, place and time. Speech normal in rate and volume, somewhat pressured when discussing work. Mood described as 'exhausted and over it'; affect congruent. Thought form coherent and logical. No delusions, hallucinations or thought disorder. Insight good and judgment intact. No psychomotor retardation or agitation."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-27",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-27",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Focused physical examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Neurologically grossly normal. Abdomen soft and non-tender with no masses. No thyroid goitre or tremor. Rest of examination unremarkable."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-28",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-28",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Targeted review of systems"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies fever, night sweats, chest pain, shortness of breath and palpitations. Denies classical thyroid symptoms, including heat or cold intolerance, tremor, and bowel habit change other than work-related loose stools. No menstrual issues volunteered."
      }
